  "Question": "In the expression \\(\\dfrac{x+1}{x-1},\\) each \\(x\\) is replaced by \\(\\dfrac{x+1}{x-1}.\\) The resulting expression, evaluated for \\(x=\\dfrac12,\\) equals:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(3\\)",
    "B": "\\(-3\\)",
    "C": "\\(1\\)",
    "D": "\\(-1\\)",
    "E": "none of these"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "Each original \\(x\\) is replaced by the whole fraction, so evaluate that replacement before evaluating the outer expression. At \\(x=1/2\\), let its value be \\(t\\). Then\n\\[\nt=\\frac{\\frac12+1}{\\frac12-1}\n=\\frac{3/2}{-1/2}=-3.\n\\]\nThe resulting expression therefore has value\n\\[\n\\frac{t+1}{t-1}\n=\\frac{-3+1}{-3-1}\n=\\frac{-2}{-4}=\\frac12.\n\\]\nThe inner denominator is \\(-1/2\\), and the outer denominator is \\(-4\\), so both evaluations are defined. Since \\(1/2\\) is absent from choices A through D, the answer is choice E.",
